[1425.546663, "o", "\u001b[1m\u001b[31merror\u001b[39m\u001b[0m\u001b[1m:\u001b[0m Failed to build `pycairo==1.29.0`\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[31mcause\u001b[39m\u001b[0m\u001b[1m:\u001b[0m The build backend returned an error\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[31mcause\u001b[39m\u001b[0m\u001b[1m:\u001b[0m Call to `mesonpy.build_wheel` failed (exit status: 1)\r\n\r\n         \u001b[31m[stderr]\u001b[39m\r\n         Traceback (most recent call last):\r\n"]
[1425.546729, "o", "           File \"<string>\", line 8, in <module>\r\n             import mesonpy as backend\r\n         ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'mesonpy'\r\n\r\n\u001b[36m\u001b[1mhint\u001b[0m\u001b[39m\u001b[1m:\u001b[0m `\u001b[36mpycairo\u001b[39m` (\u001b[36mv1.29.0\u001b[39m) was included because `\u001b[36mpychess\u001b[39m` depends on `\u001b[36mpycairo\u001b[39m`\r\n\r\n\u001b[36m\u001b[1mhint\u001b[0m\u001b[39m\u001b[1m:\u001b[0m This error likely indicates that `\u001b[36mpycairo@1.29.0\u001b[39m` depends on `\u001b[36mmeson-python\u001b[39m`, but doesn't declare it as a build dependency. If `\u001b[36mpycairo\u001b[39m` is a first-party package, consider adding `\u001b[36mmeson-python\u001b[39m` to its `\u001b[32mbuild-system.requires\u001b[39m`. Otherwise, either add it to your `pyproject.toml` under:\r\n\r\n[tool.uv.extra-build-dependencies]\r\n\u001b[36mpycairo\u001b[39m = [\"\u001b[36mmeson-python\u001b[39m\"]\r\n\r\nor `\u001b[32muv pip install meson-python\u001b[39m` into the environment and re-run with `\u001b[32m--no-build-isolation\u001b[39m`.\r\n"]
